    {
      "id": "actuator-exposure",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Expose selected endpoints"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-802e-be30-f67983df1a83",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Expose health and application information",
        "description": [
          "Use a Spring Boot 3.5 web application with spring-boot-starter-actuator.",
          "Add these settings to application.properties."
        ],
        "code": "management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=health,info\nmanagement.info.env.enabled=true\ninfo.app.name=journal-service",
        "language": "text",
        "explanation": [
          "The include list makes only health and info available over HTTP.",
          "management.info.env.enabled allows the info contributor to read info.* properties.",
          "The info endpoint includes app.name with the value journal-service.",
          "Visit /actuator/health and /actuator/info on the application’s host and port.",
          "A healthy application normally reports status UP. Health indicators can report other states."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-access",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Control access"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-access-b0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Exposing an endpoint makes it available over HTTP. It does not define who may call it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-access-b1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Restrict sensitive endpoints using Spring Security and network access rules."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-access-b2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "If you define your own SecurityFilterChain, you must include the Actuator access rules yourself."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-access-b3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Avoid exposing every endpoint with a wildcard unless access is restricted and each exposed endpoint is needed."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-monitoring",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Collect metrics"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-monitoring-b0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A metric is a numeric measurement, such as request count or elapsed time."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-monitoring-b1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Actuator uses Micrometer to collect metrics."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-monitoring-b2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Add micrometer-registry-prometheus and expose the prometheus endpoint when a Prometheus server will collect them."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-monitoring-b3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Grafana can display metrics collected by Prometheus."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "actuator-monitoring-b4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A health status or a metric does not by itself prove that every application workflow works correctly."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
